RISC-V zkVM: read an array's length with one aligned ld (applies after perf-68).

On 64-bit an SZ array's 32-bit length at offset 8 is followed by a 32-bit padding word before the
data at 16, and nothing writes that word:
- ILC emits frozen (preinitialized) arrays with it zero (TypePreinit, "padding numComponents in 64-bit");
- bflat's zkVM allocation fast paths store the length as one 64-bit word (rhp module), the runtime's
  helpers and perf-26/49's inline allocation store 32 bits into fresh memory, and the JIT
  zero-initializes a stack-allocated array before storing its header;
- a zkVM heap is fresh, zeroed RAM that is never collected or reused.
So under JitZkBumpAddr (set by bflat for every zkVM libc, never for a real riscv64 target, where a
collecting GC may hand out uninitialized memory) the length can be read as the whole aligned 64-bit
word: ld gives the length zero-extended, the same register lw and lwu give. A ZisK narrow (4-byte)
access costs a MemAlign row; an aligned ld does not. LowerArrLength marks (GTF_IND_PADDED_LENGTH) a
GT_ARR_LENGTH whose object the JIT knows is an array (CORINFO_FLG_ARRAY), never a string, whose
characters start right after its length; codegen loads it with ld, also when the load is contained
in a zero-extending cast. A load that perf-68 narrows or that strict alignment expands byte-wise keeps
its narrow form.

Nethermind stateless guest on ZisK (ziskemu 1.3.1 -X --mem-full-stats, plan from cargo-zisk execute),
block 26055159 / 26112793: steps unchanged; cost -0.17% / -0.16%; MemAlign rows -5.4% / -4.6%;
block 26112793 needs one MemAlign instance fewer (46 -> 45 instances). Outputs identical on 11
mainnet blocks.

diff --git a/src/coreclr/jit/codegenriscv64.cpp b/src/coreclr/jit/codegenriscv64.cpp
--- a/src/coreclr/jit/codegenriscv64.cpp
+++ b/src/coreclr/jit/codegenriscv64.cpp
@@ -5597,6 +5597,11 @@
         }
         gcInfo.gcMarkRegSetNpt(genRegMask(addrReg));
     }
+    else if (((tree->gtFlags & GTF_IND_PADDED_LENGTH) != 0) && (type == TYP_INT))
+    {
+        // The padding word after the length is zero (see Lowering::LowerArrLength).
+        GetEmitter()->emitInsLoadStoreOp(INS_ld, EA_8BYTE, targetReg, tree);
+    }
     else
     {
         GetEmitter()->emitInsLoadStoreOp(ins, emitActualTypeSize(type), targetReg, tree);
@@ -6498,7 +6503,9 @@
     {
         // A zero-extended INT load (see Lowering::ContainCheckCast).
         assert(cast->gtGetOp1()->OperIs(GT_IND) && cast->IsUnsigned());
-        emit->emitInsLoadStoreOp(INS_lwu, EA_4BYTE, dstReg, cast->gtGetOp1()->AsIndir());
+        GenTreeIndir* const load = cast->gtGetOp1()->AsIndir();
+        const bool padded = (load->gtFlags & GTF_IND_PADDED_LENGTH) != 0;
+        emit->emitInsLoadStoreOp(padded ? INS_ld : INS_lwu, padded ? EA_8BYTE : EA_4BYTE, dstReg, load);
         genProduceReg(cast);
         return;
     }
